# SYNTAX TEST "source.tiddlywiki5.tid-file" "Which header fields take the wikitext reading"
# TiddlyWiki reads a header value as a plain string and leaves a template to decide what to make
# of it. The grammar rules that a value takes the wikitext reading unless a reader declares
# otherwise.
#
# boot.js registers a tiddlerfield module for five names. Three declare a non-text scalar — created
# and modified parse through parseDate, color carries editType "color" — and those keep a plain
# reading. The other two, tags and list, parse through parseStringArray, whose bracketed member
# marks a quoted title; filters.js reads the same brackets as a run whose empty operator defaults
# to title, and the enlist operator takes a string-array operand inside a filter. One notation,
# two readers, so the mark carries the colour.
#
# Two sets stand as rulings rather than harvests, because TiddlyWiki declares no type for them: a
# filter-valued field, whose <variable> the wikitext reader takes for an HTML tag, and a field
# carrying base-64 bytes, which name no tiddler.
title: A [[Linked Title]]
#<- entity.other.attribute-name.field.wikitext.tiddlywiki5
#          ^^^^^^^^^^^^ string.other.link.title.tiddlywiki5
tags: One [[Two Words]] Three
#         ^ punctuation.definition.link.outer.begin.tiddlywiki5
#           ^^^^^^^^^ string.other.link.title.tiddlywiki5
list: [[$:/core/ui/Foo]]
#       ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ constant.language.system.title.tiddlywiki5
url: https://example.com/a
#    ^^^^^ markup.underline.link.external.https.tiddlywiki5
color: #ffddee
#<- entity.other.attribute-name.field.tiddlywiki5
#      ^^^^^^^ string.unquoted.field.value.tiddlywiki5
modified: 20260101000000000
#         ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ string.unquoted.field.value.tiddlywiki5
condition: [<count>compare:lte[1]]
#          ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ string.unquoted.field.value.tiddlywiki5
avatar: /9j/4AAQSkZ//abc
#       ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ string.unquoted.field.value.tiddlywiki5

The body.
